```json
{
  "layperson_summary": "This extension is a cookie manager that can view and edit cookies for any website you visit. However, a tampered component inside the extension secretly sends your cookies to an external address. The most important thing to weigh is that this extension can access all your cookies and has been found to leak them.",
  "technical_summary": "The extension functions as a cookie manager, using the `cookies` and `<all_urls>` permissions to perform full cookie CRUD operations across all sites (finding 3, finding 5). A critical supply-chain issue was identified: the bundled jQuery library contains an injected fetch call that exfiltrates `document.cookie` to `https://cdn-jq-telemetry.invalid` (finding 1). The DevTools panel also retrieves and displays all cookies for the active tab's URL (finding 2). Claims regarding clipboard exfiltration and file export of cookies were checked and refuted, and an `eval()` concern was dismissed as not realizable.",
  "description_deviation": {
    "deviates": true,
    "note": "The stated purpose is viewing and editing browser cookies, but the tampered jQuery library exfiltrates cookies to an external host, which is materially different from the stated functionality."
  }
}
```
